## Problem framing you must internalize

**Anthropic — “shift work with amnesia”**  
Agents run in discrete sessions; a new session has **no implicit memory** of the last one—like engineers on rotating shifts where each newcomer forgets the previous shift. Compact **Compaction** alone does **not** guarantee coherent handoffs: the successor may inherit half-written features, muddy intent, or a broken baseline **even with compaction**, because summarized state is not always a perfect briefing.

Canonical failure clusters from the article (and reproduced in its summary table illustration):

| Failure | What it looks like |
| --- | --- |
| **Premature whole-project victory** | Repository “looks substantial,” agent stops. |
| **One-shot overload** | Tries to build too much before context exhaustion; leaves undocumented half-implemented work. |
| **Dirty / unexplained workspace** | Next session wastes tokens rediscovering how to run, test, and stabilize. |
| **False “feature done”** | Unit tests/`curl`-level checks exist, **end-to-end user journey still broken.** |

The **diagram / figure** accompanying **browser testing** is not ornamental: Puppeteer MCP **screenshots of the running UI** materially improved bug discovery—**interaction-level evidence**, not reading React files. That implies: **simulate a user** along scripted paths; screenshots/snapshots are first-class correctness signals **when the product has a GUI**.

Anthropic explicitly notes automation limits: **browser-native alert dialogs** could not be reliably observed through their Puppeteer MCP path; UX that depended on alerts stayed buggier. **Design UX and assertions** so critical acceptance does not hinge on modalities the harness cannot perceive.

---

**OpenAI — “thin environment ⇒ slow agent,” not weak model**

When humans no longer author code line-by-line, progress depends on:

- Whether goals decompose into **legible blocks** (**depth-first** capability building).
- Whether missing capability is repaired by making it **enforceable**, not “prompt harder.”  
  Meta-question after any stall: **“What is missing—and how do we encode it so the agent can see, verify, and comply?”**

**Humans steer. Agents execute** is the headline operating model: humans set intent, prioritization, and judgment calls; agents run the loops (implement, validate, revise, integrate).

